            <div xml:id="d212">

                <pb facs="0277" n="269" sameAs="frus:frus1941v07/pg269"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.20 Defense/1793: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Ecuador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Long</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Quito</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-12-16T21:00:00-05:00">December 16, 1941—9
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 10:50 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>543. My number 538 of December 15, 7 p.m. Notes exchanged today. Ecuador accepts
                    all measures proposed in Department’s telegram number 387 of December 13, 8
                        p.m.<anchor n="33" xml:id="d212-f1"/> Copies of notes follow via next air
                        mail.<anchor n="34" xml:id="d212-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Long</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
